course: dictionary
lesson: 2494
title: One word, two kinds of meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and a capital letter can be a clue. Dean with a small d is a job. Dean with a big D is a name. Context tells you which one the writer means.
explain: Read «The teacher talks to Dean and his parents.» Dean has a capital letter and it sits beside «his parents», so it is a boy's name, not a job. Ask: does the sentence make sense if Dean is a person's name?
explain: Now read «Dean has had it in for Sam since Year 2.» Dean is the one who has a grudge against Sam, so Dean is a character. When you meet a name you don't know, read on: the sentences around it tell you who the person is and what they do.
fact: A dean is a person in charge of part of a college or university, or in charge of students.
fact: A dean can also be a leader of priests in a large church.
fact: Dean with a capital D is a boy's name or a family name.
fact: In «In Year 2 Sam knocked over Dean's Lego tower by accident», Dean is a name, and the apostrophe shows the tower belongs to Dean.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The teacher talks to Dean and his parents.» Is Dean a name or a job here? | A kind of tower | *A name | A job in charge of a college | A leader of priests
exercise: «Dean has had it in for Sam since Year 2.» Who is Dean? | A dean giving out prizes at a college | Sam's teacher | A leader of priests in a large church | *The boy who has a grudge against Sam
exercise: What does a dean mean? | A pupil who sits at the front | *A person in charge of part of a college or university | A type of Lego brick | A river in a big city
test: In «In Year 2 Sam knocked over Dean's Lego tower by accident», what is Dean? | A dean at a university | A priest | *A boy's name, and the owner of the tower | A tower of bricks
test: «Next day Dean mutters «ta» (thanks) and leaves him alone.» What does «ta» mean here? | A goodbye | *Thanks | Stop | A type of prize
exam: Which of these is a meaning of dean? | A type of bread | A loud noise in a music hall | *A person in charge of students at a college | A kind of dog's bark
